@lang en
-- These materials contain information that has been derived from information originally made available by the Province of British Columbia at: http://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca and this information is being used in accordance with the King's Printer Licence – British Columbia available at: https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/standards/Licence.html. They have not, however, been produced in affiliation with, or with the endorsement of, the Province of British Columbia and THESE MATERIALS ARE NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION.
--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-time.l4: what a holiday, or a day an office is closed, does to the
-- beginning or end of a period (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238,
-- ss 25(3), 25(4), 25.5 and 29 "holiday").
--
-- The calendar is an INPUT. The text fixes only two kinds of holiday by their date: every Sunday
-- and every December 26 (s 29 "holiday", paras (a) and (c)). It names the others (Christmas Day,
-- Good Friday, Easter Monday, ...) without giving dates, so this file supplies a calendar of its
-- own, in the function `test calendar: other holidays`, and claims nothing about the real one.
-- Saturday is not in the text's list, so it is not a holiday here.
--
-- Weekdays, worked out by hand from the calendar: 2026-01-31 is a Saturday; 2026-04-03 Friday,
-- 04-04 Saturday, 04-05 Sunday, 04-06 Monday, 04-07 Tuesday; 2026-12-25 Friday, 12-26 Saturday,
-- 12-27 Sunday, 12-28 Monday.
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and was written down before the first run.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`

GIVETH A `Position of the reference day`
`ref before the period` MEANS `The reference day is before the period`

GIVETH A `Position of the reference day`
`ref after the period` MEANS `The reference day is after the period`

-- Supplied by this test: Friday 3 April 2026 and Monday 6 April 2026 (so Sunday 5 April sits
-- between two holidays), and Friday 25 December 2026.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test calendar: other holidays` d MEANS
        d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3
    OR  d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
    OR  d EQUALS YMD 2026 12 25

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test calendar: a day is a holiday` d MEANS
    `s 29 a day is a holiday` `test calendar: other holidays` d

-- An office open Monday to Friday, closed on Friday 3 April 2026 for a reason that is not its
-- regular closing, and regularly closed on Saturday and Sunday.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test office: open during regular business hours` d MEANS
        (`Weekday of` d AT LEAST 1 AND `Weekday of` d AT MOST 5)
    AND NOT (d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test office: regularly closed` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d EQUALS 0 OR `Weekday of` d EQUALS 6

-- The text's own holidays and nothing else: Sundays and 26 December.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test calendar: only the days the text names` d MEANS
    `s 29 a day is a holiday` (GIVEN x YIELD FALSE) d

§ `s 29 holiday`

#ASSERT `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 5)
#ASSERT `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 12 26)
#ASSERT `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2025 12 26)
#ASSERT `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 3)
#ASSERT `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 12 25)
#ASSERT NOT (`test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4))
#ASSERT NOT (`test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 7))
#ASSERT NOT (`test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 1 31))

§ `s 25(3)(a) reference day before the period: the next day that is not a holiday`

-- Sunday 5 April and Monday 6 April are holidays in a row: the period ends on Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- Monday 6 April, a holiday followed by a Tuesday.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 6) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- Friday 3 April, a holiday followed by a Saturday, which is not a holiday: the next day is Saturday.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
-- Not a holiday: unchanged.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 7) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- Three in a row: Friday 25 December (supplied), Saturday 26 December (by the text), Sunday 27 December (by the text).
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 12 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 28

§ `s 25(3)(b) reference day after the period: the previous day that is not a holiday`

#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
-- Monday 6 April and Sunday 5 April, holidays in a row: back to Saturday 4 April.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 6) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 2
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 12 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 28
-- Three in a row backward: Sunday 27, Saturday 26, Friday 25 December; Thursday 24 December is free.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 12 27) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 24

§ `s 25(3) applies to periods of days, weeks, months and years (ss 25.2, 25.3 and 25.4)`

-- 30 days from 6 March 2026 end on Sunday 5 April (25 days to 31 March, 5 more).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 3 6) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- 4 weeks from Sunday 8 March 2026: 28 days, Sunday 5 April.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of weeks counted from a day` (YMD 2026 3 8) 4 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 8) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks, `how many` IS 4, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- 1 month from 5 March 2026 ends on 5 April.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 3 5) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 5) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- 1 year from 5 April 2025 ends on 5 April 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2025 4 5) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2025 4 5) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
-- Backward: the beginning of the period one month before 6 May 2026 is 6 April, a holiday, and moves earlier.
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
-- A period that ends on a Saturday is not moved: Saturday is not in the text's list of holidays.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

§ `Whether a day is inside a period for doing an act`

-- 30 days from 6 March 2026: without the holiday rule the period ends on 5 April, with it on 7 April.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 7) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 8) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 7) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 6) (YMD 2026 3 6) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))
-- Backward: one month before 6 May 2026, the period for doing an act begins on 4 April.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 3) (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 5 5) (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 5 6) (YMD 2026 5 6) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))

§ `s 25(3) "begins or ends": the day next to the reference day moves off a holiday too`

-- s 25(3) speaks of a period that "begins or ends" on a holiday, so the near end moves as well as
-- the far end (NOTES, fork F-near-end). The calendar is the one above: Sunday 5 April and Monday
-- 6 April 2026 are holidays in a row.
-- One day from Saturday 4 April: counting starts on Sunday 5 April, a holiday. Both ends move to
-- Tuesday 7 April, and the period is that one day.
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 7) (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 8) (YMD 2026 4 4) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
-- 30 days from Saturday 7 March: counting starts on Sunday 8 March (a holiday), so the period
-- begins on Monday 9 March; day 30 is Monday 6 April (a holiday), so it ends on Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 3 7) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 7) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 7) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 8) (YMD 2026 3 7) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 3 9) (YMD 2026 3 7) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
-- Backward: 3 days before Tuesday 7 April. Counting back from Monday 6 April: 6 April is day 1,
-- 5 April day 2, 4 April day 3, so the far end (the beginning) is Saturday 4 April, not a holiday.
-- The near end, 6 April, is a holiday, and so is 5 April: it moves back to Saturday 4 April.
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` 3 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4) (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period for doing an act` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 3) (YMD 2026 4 7) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 3, `clear` IS FALSE))

§ `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act`

#ASSERT `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 7
#ASSERT `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 4 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: a day is a holiday` (YMD 2026 12 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 28

§ `s 25(4) and s 25.5(2) a business office that is not open`

-- (a) the next day the office is open: from Saturday 4 April the office is shut on Sunday and
-- opens on Monday 6 April.
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
-- (b) the office is regularly closed on the day AND the reference day is after the period: the
-- previous day it is open. Saturday 4 April: Friday 3 April is shut (not regularly), so Thursday 2 April.
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 2
-- A Sunday boundary with the reference day after the period: Saturday is shut, Friday 10 April is open.
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 12) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 10
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 12) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 13
-- Shut on Friday 3 April but NOT regularly closed: even with the reference day after the period,
-- limb (b) does not apply (it needs BOTH conditions), so the next day the office is open,
-- Monday 6 April. This differs from s 25(3)(b), which looks back whenever the reference day is after.
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
-- An open day is unchanged.
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 8) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 8
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` `test office: regularly closed` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 8) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 8
-- s 25.5(2): a day specified for doing an act in a business office.
#ASSERT `s 25.5(2) a day specified for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` (YMD 2026 4 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `s 25.5(2) a day specified for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` (YMD 2026 4 3) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
#ASSERT `s 25.5(2) a day specified for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` `test office: open during regular business hours` (YMD 2026 4 8) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 8

§ `A calendar that leaves no free day`

-- A calendar that says every day is a holiday, or that every day the office is shut, cannot be
-- walked to the end: after 366 days the walk refuses (the text does not say what then).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` (GIVEN x YIELD TRUE) `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 5)
        BECAUSE "the holiday calendar supplied has no day free of holidays within a year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` (GIVEN x YIELD TRUE) `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 5)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(4) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act in a business office, moved to a day the office is open` (GIVEN x YIELD FALSE) `test office: regularly closed` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 5)
        BECAUSE "the office calendar supplied has no open day within a year"

§ `The calendar passed in is the whole calendar`

-- The functions that take a holiday calendar apply exactly the calendar they are given. A
-- calendar that says "never a holiday" leaves Sunday 5 April alone, although s 29 names Sunday:
-- the text's own Sundays and 26 December come from `s 29 a day is a holiday`, which the caller
-- must apply (NOTES, "Calling the time module"). This test pins that behaviour down.
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` (GIVEN x YIELD FALSE) `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` (GIVEN x YIELD FALSE) `ref after the period` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the beginning or end of a period for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test calendar: only the days the text names` `ref before the period` (YMD 2026 4 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
